  "label": "Stereotype: Women 'Taking Over' Men's Spaces",
  "description": "A misogynistic trope that implies women are 'taking over' spaces traditionally dominated by men. The phrase 'when she finally has your own month' implies a woman is 'taking' a month that was 'yours,' which can be interpreted as a misogynistic framing, even if not explicitly about gender, it reinforces the idea of 'taking' a space that belongs to a man.",
